  "heading_path": [
    "Trade Marks Regulations 1995",
    "Part 3A—Assisted filing service",
    "Division 2—Request for filing assistance",
    "3A.4  AFS request—assessment by Registrar"
  ],
  "instrument": "TMR1995",
  "kind": "regulation",
  "number": "3A.4",
  "ref": "TMR1995/r3A.4",
  "text": "(1) After receiving an AFS request the Registrar must, as soon as practicable, assess the AFS request having regard to the requirements of Part 4 of the Act and form an opinion whether or not: (a) the AFS request would, if submitted in that form as an application for registration under Part 4 of the Act, be in accordance with that Part; and (b) there would be grounds under Division 2 of Part 4 of the Act for rejecting the AFS request. (2) After forming an opinion the Registrar must, as soon as practicable, inform the requester of: (a) the opinion; and (b) the procedural requirements of regulation 3A.5 for making an amendment to the AFS request; and (c) the procedural requirements for making an application for the registration of a trade mark under Part 4 of the Act. (3) The Registrar may inform the requester: (a) in writing, by mail, fax or email; or (b) by telephone; or (c) in person.",
  "title": "AFS request—assessment by Registrar",
